\
Keygen\
- Signing Nodes produce keyshares\
- FROST key share encrypted and attested to THOR, allowing emergency recovery (same as ECDA and EDDSA)\
- Birthday saved on-chain \
\
\
Inbounds\
- Observed: inbound is observed to view key\
- Finalized: key image produced + validated (1-block) OR conf-counting limit applies, so could be 1+ blocks up to max 30\
- Non-signing Nodes: wait\
- Signing nodes coordinate to produce the key image + signature\
- key image + signature is propagated in the attestation, non-signing nodes verify key image + signature and attest\
- Observation must carry key image (signature is discarded), thus key-images on THOR are valid and final \
- key images accrue in the vault\
- key image ceremonies are TOP priority\
\
Outbounds\
- Observed: outbound in monero mempool on on-chain with txkey\
- Finalized: key-image for CHANGE output produced and validated (1-block). If no change output, then no key-image needed\
- Leader appointed, starts session\
- Joiners join, begin\
- CHANGE is always returned to SELF (OUT, REFUND, CONSOLIDATE, MIGRATE)\
- Signers attest with txkey\
- Non-signers validate txkey and attest (first observation). Txkey is discarded if valid. \
- Signers wait one block, then see the inbound (CHANGE) \
- Inbound is processed (if coming from SELF, then signers realise it\'92s already Observed, need Finalisation, so kick of key-image-gen)\
- Nonsigning nodes validate key image and attest \
\
Change\
- Monero outputs minimum two\
- All outbounds: change goes to SELF\
- If final Migration Sweep, (or there is no change) then 0-output second output to same recipient \
- 0-outputs can be ignored for key-image-gen\
\
CONSOLIDATE\
- Every 15 outputs, consolidate down to 1 output\
- second output is 0-amount can be ignored for key-image-gen \
\
0-output CHANGE, 2 cases\
- CONSOLIDATE\
- FINAL MIGRATE\
- ignore key-image-gen for this output\
\
\
RESCAN MODE\
- Important to repair inventory (Inbounds, SPENT or UNSPENT == TOTAL BALANCE)\
- Get ViewKey, PubKeys, Birthdays, Keyimages from THOR, save per-vault\
- Scan Monero Daemon, find Inbounds and Spent Keyimages\
- Inbounds are SPENT or UNSPENT, contain hash + amount\
- Keyimages are PENDING or applied to an Inbound, if applied, Inbound is SPENT\
- total balance can be validated on EVERY Node, Signing or Non-signing (don\'92t rely on scanner balance view, it won\'92t be correct for watch-only vaults)\
- reconcile() takes all PENDING Keyimages and applies to found Inbounds (iterate)\
- if spent key image found first before Inbound, no worries, a later reconcile() will pick it up and apply\
- reconcile() called after batch in rescan or block in normal \
\
NORMAL MODE\
- no work stream if not yet at tip\
- at tip when scan for all vaults is at tip\
- rescan is only finding inbounds + spent keyimages and reconciling them\
- Signing Nodes produce key-images + signatures and attest, Non-signing Nodes validate and attest just with key image and inbound\
- All nodes can cache keyimage-signatures, but signatures are not attested to THOR. Finalization only happens if validated, so inbounds finalized on THOR means correct validation\
\
\
Old Vault Refunds\
- Active Nodes continue to attest to inbounds to old vaults\
- If enough active nodes finalize  an inbound (67% of active) then it can be processed, default is REFUND\
- if user did not add a REFUND address, then can\'92t refund, sweep\
- in this case, sweep by NOOP:NOVAULT to latest vault (add to vault accounting, not pool accounting)\
- In this case, some Signing nodes will be Standby Signing Nodes, they need to join keysign ceremony even if Standby\
- REFUND or sweep tx needs txkey \
- Inbound to new Vault needs to be handled \
\
\
REORG\
- if monero reorgs and an inbound or outbound disappears\
- nodes will see, need to do ERRATA\
- ERRATA will undo the inbound/outbound and reverse the accounting\
- delete keyimages associated with that inbound (or change output from outbound)\
